{"title":"2023 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An arithmetic sequence of positive integers has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e2533d6abdb11a9a1626c0240fab1a9200fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> terms, initial term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and common difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/97256277ca68f80f48c1e0b392e04f1b26d46bfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />. Carl wrote down all the terms in this sequence correctly except for one term, which was off by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The sum of the terms he wrote was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/155fa3807f26f4268430319bb47b97658353ad8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$222$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04d458bfd49f697318d4ee15d1f84c23e7d6610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + d + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d75a8c5a5fc7f2da9a3806406bf19739521c6d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 24 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 20 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 22 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 28 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since one of the terms was either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />  more or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less than it should have been, the sum should have been <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/16358222255dfea640bc9b42f5d146dd5602bdb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$222-1=221$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad3914fb1555ffe0818be94c09339e88987c52c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$222+1=223.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p>The formula for an arithmetic series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/08708d526c04acb2db8c11887a25114cc9fa769a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$an+d\\left(\\dfrac{(n-1)n}2\\right)=\\dfrac n2\\left(2a+d(n-1)\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"326\" height=\"45\" /> This can quickly be rederived by noticing that the sequence goes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c4e2169a777e592a8800033928c0e4945a9c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,a+d,a+2d,a+3d,\\dots,a+(n-1)d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"316\" height=\"20\" />, and grouping terms. \n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3fdbe73f7b00438b25ac2d78802b2759f93eb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac n2(2a+d(n-1))=221$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"34\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Let us now show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is not possible. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d6881c0b62b0a87118d0b793051f72fad9ec809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac n2(2a+d(n-1))=223$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"189\" height=\"34\" />, we can simplify this to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416950f2db0e5c988feb3b42ca5ac3a31a735011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(2a+d(n-1))=223\\cdot2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" /> Since every expression here should be an integer, we know that either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/2/7a2f9b718866575344f031193915b8a65c379b29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+d(n-1)=223$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/64327436c995276bad5466efcb23ec72b23400c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=223$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21beb7257a9ed7161461651cdb4867f05978d851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+d(n-1)=2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" /> The latter is not possible, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f6709c2f26ce5dba0b4ecfaa0c97df9781a286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge3,d&gt;1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/7/3470668bb8a39eebcb9ed22863d4c71245731ed9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> The former is also impossible, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38ca8e5235c3edab27fe1290742bbee8a2966b03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21d2a16d02983f4e91bd018f4a2dba52266f2d6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac n2(2a+d(n-1))\\neq223\\implies\\dfrac n2(2a+d(n-1))=221$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"426\" height=\"34\" />. \n</p><p>(Alternatively, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79a22e3bdc5aff50a597f7b50d975778d1efe0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms and arithmetic mean <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d3c78b0e64ac444bc83be167b839ae3623aa61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223=mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" /> does not satisfy both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cce1bd621aff652b0983cbc94a24545e5f4bdcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d98ffe996c0f0d3b82b284cba2113439fefea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> because it is prime.)\n</p><p>We can factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/7/5a72f3c9fddcede20d6d6a626a973a42d7b3f541.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13\\cdot17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. Using similar reasoning, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/b/8cba29ad4a571a5ac6debe45c2756c3853dcafdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221\\cdot2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be paired as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, but rather must be paired as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> with a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> somewhere. \n</p><p>Let us first try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf1cd3d46634467dd8a7381f47dd63cc461ee96e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=13.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> Our equation simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/938c29d8fd610a1ba2dd6bf56d8f4cbd28fef57c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a+12d=34\\implies a+6d=17.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"260\" height=\"16\" /> We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c2ec9427a1622ec2e68274be50812c1893eba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&gt;1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> so we try the smallest possible value: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c862f1a7fb3753d93eb8c7dc1996057cb3b74663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=2.$\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> This would give us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/f/86f679bf00711198ea292693d9316b397ff9f67b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=17-2\\cdot6=17-12=5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"229\" height=\"15\" /> (Indeed, this is the only possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.)\n</p><p>There is nothing wrong with the values we have achieved, so it is reasonable to assume that this is the only valid solution (or all solutions sum to the same thing), so we answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/5/0f588f3f1eea81f154fbef752fdd3e4004aad450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d+n=5+2+13=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"275\" height=\"30\" /> \n</p><p>For the sake of completeness, we can explore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/7/427575c17fea2d990457a446032c169ad447c7a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=17.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> It turns out that we reach a contradiction in this case, so we are done. \n</p><p>~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> terms, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />th term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/95644844ccc1267334ec1321dea88754a45b6a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+(x-1)d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" />, so the summation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/2/37278d40f9dc0319288d2b81eb0fc94c4b8d419b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$an+dn(n-1)/2=n(a+\\frac{d(n-1)}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"290\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe summation of the set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/b/cdb70f67796268a20a6d1c433152778ba9b9b83c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$222 \\pm 1 = 221,223$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is a prime number, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is the only other option. First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />: its only possible factors are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0fe8ed20edcc2565caae6951e905edfa9f0196.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,13,17,221$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />, and as said by the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b21b36bfc3bad4b81f5aed2c6f5613bc98403ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbbf15f8660697080876a2ecab58d0dbba21b52b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13,17,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Let's start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608f4cbd198d2af6bf20b99fc5e126469e09ec84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d949d5a8d0badabaabdc952f7839d1ea0d1069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+6d=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53897e4b47f6049266b4bffcef91bc949385b5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/588e07a0cfc1e617ac5d6552a759b3011aa96d6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Summing gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/c/16cc4e0d520020bc8ebcd6bf8b71fede3c27180f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13+5+2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"171\" height=\"30\" />. We don't need to test any more cases, since the problem writes that all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc62c963c4ad6b23a9f93dfbda9cd8e259656d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" /> are the same.\n</p><p>-HIA2020\n</p><p>minor edits by Lunar_paradox\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We must have the sum of terms of the arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a00704fb8b3226afc39ac9fb4456026d00177b6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$222\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Since we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is prime, it cannot be the sum of the arithmetic sequence.\n</p><p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95bddc932f561a69861093e7f1b907ba3861e3e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13\\times 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We can write any arithmetic sequence with an odd amount of terms like this:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/f/56f1bb0364b3b8e4b87a3b7f97452b1fba65cd7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-md,\\cdots ,b-2d,b-d,b,b+d,b+2d,\\cdots b+md$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"405\" height=\"18\" /> where b is the middle term and d is the common difference.\n</p><p>By the sum of an arithmetic sequence, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/2630243283e63edb24c6926288b9fcee07d88fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13b=221$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/6109dd4f2131d3f9549ead2350f30a8cc5d4fc77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17b=221$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/497d608362a3d135b9d6d7a9dac945053e07612a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5eb8726a34932d28103ce7ce17456421222603f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/158cb69c9e770ffbfc6bfe2731763720b029f75f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(13,17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/5/075547c1fab2acb2f49dba27b93170037bd2573a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(17,13)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/9284e4a21e0c0ef8292a0cc9f555012ba03a9f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d+n=b-md+d+n=30-(m-1)d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"356\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We must have that m is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96ec017fe8cae018156405b3019c586f3bfc8bfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{17-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/b/7eb7ef8451c45931d08f2d369b7e50f0a21e21bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" />, so m is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e2fc8b3fe366bc6d912453800f21abfd2e25f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d+n=30-5d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26f00c123aba62840d0750fecac4058d9af264f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-7d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Taking<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e4461877e328edd4298545f51c7d8d170bd3bed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod 7$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, we have no answer choices that give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and then taking<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d295e09ce09aaac8f2731db9a74b49a22c0566a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod 5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> gives the only answer that works is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39bf7deea8a57245b7e92ee3799a6d08bb2eb7e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d+n=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"170\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ESAOPS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula for the sum of an arithmetic sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca93a75039cedbf78070934c525ac52df003bc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(\\frac{a_1+a_n}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the first term, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is the last term, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of terms. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the first term, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the common difference, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of terms of Carl's sequence. Since the sum the sequence is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> less or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/155fa3807f26f4268430319bb47b97658353ad8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$222$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/38209a054128921057a31ff13855ed1d6f41be61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n(\\frac{a+d(n-1)}{2})\\pm{1} = 222\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807ffd88a3e5f42e58a7fb799c812a7cf18c53cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n(\\frac{a+d(n-1)}{2}) = 222\\pm{1}.\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"38\" />\nThe right-hand side is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. We know that it has to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> so we can find the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. Checking all the primes less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/472004076edfc8b47b0f4e9b7cfb4af70104bec5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$223$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is prime and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18c4f9d64dcee9c0b4fe2fe6ce7a31ead541465c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221=13\\cdot17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b21b36bfc3bad4b81f5aed2c6f5613bc98403ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, the sum must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f490c9585fc04684a97f897f87d49d972658089a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$221$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and the only possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We can test both cases. \n</p><p><br />\nCase 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e5a50f89eb87941facbb1e7b1ae91777fa10f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />\nSubstituting for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/8/688981e6ebeda8736bfeea4233eaf48be3ed1f7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+8d=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />. Since the sequence consists of only positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/b/ffbab47ac6155c011021cbf97c17e0a1fece0ff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> but if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/39880deb2d7e0fa775f903acdf08fff0713420fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\ge2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd72654690c94c4adca2aaed06d22da254177360.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8d&gt;13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />. Hence, this case is not possible. \n</p><p><br />\nCase 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608f4cbd198d2af6bf20b99fc5e126469e09ec84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />\nSubstituting for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d949d5a8d0badabaabdc952f7839d1ea0d1069f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+6d=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />. Using the same logic from case 1, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/78895a1ead220b920f8b93d83cae95021cb7a692.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3&gt;d&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/588e07a0cfc1e617ac5d6552a759b3011aa96d6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53897e4b47f6049266b4bffcef91bc949385b5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f5146584ce524a0271c19349334149687c352766.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+d+n=5+2+13=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b66f44cb4a84481effd7cfbc9ac0e5be6d2880c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }20.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" /> .\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F30LJeoaNWo\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F30LJeoaNWo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/IDYnZmNh1io\">https://youtu.be/IDYnZmNh1io</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-